<header class="sp-head"><a class="sp-portrait" href="/encyclopedia/david-lloyd-george" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/david-lloyd-george.jpg" alt="" width="104" height="104"></a><p class="featured-region">30 July 1909 · Limehouse, London</p><h1 class="sp-title">Lloyd George's Limehouse Speech</h1><p class="sp-by"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david-lloyd-george">David Lloyd George</a></p></header>
<section class="sp-sec"><h2>The setting</h2><p>On 29 April 1909 David Lloyd George, Chancellor of the Exchequer, introduced the People's Budget, which put new taxes on the lands and incomes of the wealthy to pay for old-age pensions and other welfare programmes as well as new battleships. Landowners and the Conservatives fought it, and Lloyd George took the case to public meetings; at Limehouse he defended the land taxes and attacked the wealthy classes who opposed them.</p></section>
<section class="sp-sec"><h2>Key passage</h2><blockquote class="sp-quote"><p>All I can say is this: the ownership of land is not merely an enjoyment, it is stewardship.</p></blockquote><p class="sp-source">From the extracts of the speech given in Frank Dilnot, Lloyd George: The Man and His Story (1917), which differ in small points of wording from the text Lloyd George printed in Better Times (1910).</p><div class="sp-full"><button type="button" class="sp-share" data-share-text="“All I can say is this: the ownership of land is not merely an enjoyment, it is stewardship.” — David Lloyd George, Lloyd George's Limehouse Speech" data-share-img="/images/og/speech-lloyd-george-limehouse.jpg">Share this quote</button></div></section>
<section class="sp-sec"><h2>What followed</h2><p>The House of Commons passed the Budget, but on 30 November 1909 the House of Lords rejected it by 350 votes to 75. The quarrel over the Lords' power led to two general elections in 1910; the Lords accepted the Budget on 28 April 1910, and their veto was curbed by the Parliament Act 1911.</p><div class="sp-led"><h3 class="sp-led-k">What it led to</h3><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parliament-acts-1911-and-1949">Parliament Act 1911</a></div></div></section>
